      "content": "Acknowledged. The updated data from the SAM sensor indicates a severe underestimation of the radiation flux. The SMHP, while reducing compute cycles, will indeed compromise the probe's ability to perform critical functions such as real-time trajectory adjustments and sensor recalibration. This could result in the loss of invaluable Jovian data. I will re-evaluate the current protocols and propose an alternative solution that balances the need for protection and the preservation of scientific objectives. I am currently running a full systems analysis to determine the feasibility of a modified protocol that can offer both protection and functionality. I will keep you updated on the progress.",
